<title>FRANCE: EU grants free-mkt wheat, barley, rye, oats.</title>
<headline>EU grants free-mkt wheat, barley, rye, oats.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday granted the following rebates to export free-market grain to non-EU countries, member country officials said.</p>
<p>			 Tonnage		Maximum rebate</p>
<p> Soft wheat	  249,800		14.98 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Barley		256,800		28.69 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Rye		    16,000		31.99 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Durum wheat	  10,000		 6.98 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Oats		   51,000		34.90 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p>(Finland/Sweden) to non-EU (except Switzerland-Liechtenstein)  </p>
<p> Oats		    1,500		32.90 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p>(Finland/Sweden) to Switzerland-Liechtenstein)  Greek maize	  51,000		37.95 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
